WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.269 --> 00:00:04.560
something really interesting going on in the
youtube space over the last week or so.

00:00:04.560 --> 00:00:06.710
You might know that for the last couple of
of years

00:00:06.710 --> 00:00:11.260
there have been struggles on youtube that
the David Pakman show channel has experienced.

00:00:11.260 --> 00:00:14.090
The first one was back in April of 2017.

00:00:14.090 --> 00:00:19.740
Back then we were sort of a middle of the
road size channel and uh, we've also struggled

00:00:19.740 --> 00:00:21.820
more recently in some other areas.

00:00:21.820 --> 00:00:26.830
Now we are sort of in the top one or 2% of
Youtube and the struggles that we're having

00:00:26.830 --> 00:00:30.210
now are pretty different from the ones that
we were having a couple of years ago.

00:00:30.210 --> 00:00:35.920
As a result of different algorithm, algorithmic
and advertising related changes to the platform.

00:00:35.920 --> 00:00:40.200
And very often whenever I talk about youtube
woes, people will write to me and they'll

00:00:40.200 --> 00:00:45.320
say, Hey David, you should unionize on youtube
so that all of you channels could bargain

00:00:45.320 --> 00:00:49.140
together with youtube for monetization and
status.

00:00:49.140 --> 00:00:53.530
And I've actually spoken to entertainment
lawyers about this casually.

00:00:53.530 --> 00:00:58.040
And typically what they say is that youtube
is set up legally in the United States.

00:00:58.040 --> 00:01:05.409
Uh, in a way that current law would not easily
allow a unionization of Youtube burrs without

00:01:05.409 --> 00:01:10.170
wholesale changes to the law regarding independent
contractors and employees and a whole bunch

00:01:10.170 --> 00:01:11.909
of other things.

00:01:11.909 --> 00:01:17.470
However, European law is different and there
is a huge movement in Europe for a whole bunch

00:01:17.470 --> 00:01:23.369
of youtubers to unionize and to bargain collectively
for light rights with Youtube.

00:01:23.369 --> 00:01:27.520
So this is potentially huge and I'm going
to talk about it in detail, but before we

00:01:27.520 --> 00:01:30.750
even get into that, I also need to be very
honest with you.

00:01:30.750 --> 00:01:35.289
I don't think I'd be interested in being a
part of this youtube or as union at this point

00:01:35.289 --> 00:01:38.720
in time based on our challenge size.

00:01:38.720 --> 00:01:42.869
On our channel size, and I'll explain to you
why I support unions.

00:01:42.869 --> 00:01:47.990
I think collective bargaining is a great way
for individual players to get more clout and

00:01:47.990 --> 00:01:50.359
have more control over their circumstances.

00:01:50.359 --> 00:01:51.859
I support teachers' unions.

00:01:51.859 --> 00:01:58.490
I support factory workers, unions and transportation
workers, unionizing and pilots, sports league

00:01:58.490 --> 00:02:00.679
players, the whole thing.

00:02:00.679 --> 00:02:06.200
But that being said right now, given that
my channel is one of the, you know, in the

00:02:06.200 --> 00:02:12.020
top one or 2% of Youtube, I don't believe
it would be to my advantage to get into a

00:02:12.020 --> 00:02:18.010
union unless it's a union of news and politics,
Youtube burrs that are my size or larger,

00:02:18.010 --> 00:02:20.140
which are relatively few.

00:02:20.140 --> 00:02:27.150
And what I mean by that is now that my channel
is run as a part of a broader business that

00:02:27.150 --> 00:02:31.020
is very different than what it was even two
years ago when we had a couple hundred thousand

00:02:31.020 --> 00:02:38.900
subscribers, there is no way that a consortium
or a union of channels that are not just using

00:02:38.900 --> 00:02:43.870
politics that are everything from makeup and
gaming and sports and whatever else, uh, and

00:02:43.870 --> 00:02:46.120
drastically different sizes.

00:02:46.120 --> 00:02:52.010
There's no way that it would be to my advantage
to be in that union because our needs and

00:02:52.010 --> 00:02:58.760
our circumstances are now so different than
those of the majority of youtube channels.

00:02:58.760 --> 00:03:03.090
Now you might hear me say this and react by
saying, oh, David, that's because your channel

00:03:03.090 --> 00:03:04.090
is successful.

00:03:04.090 --> 00:03:07.290
That's, that's why I mean I'm recognizing
that I'm not denying it.

00:03:07.290 --> 00:03:11.660
I want the full freedom to do or not do anything
I want on Youtube.

00:03:11.660 --> 00:03:16.900
I want the freedom to put my content or not
on any other platforms that I want.

00:03:16.900 --> 00:03:22.800
I am actually at the point where only a union
of the top news and politics channels would

00:03:22.800 --> 00:03:28.780
actually be useful and that would arguably
defeat the kind of egalitarian nature of the

00:03:28.780 --> 00:03:33.500
union to begin with because the truth is that
at this point, even if youtube screws me,

00:03:33.500 --> 00:03:37.370
I don't know that being part of a union like
the one in Europe would benefit me.

00:03:37.370 --> 00:03:39.420
This is why I left TYT network years ago.

00:03:39.420 --> 00:03:43.660
It had nothing to do with conflict with TYT
of any kind.

00:03:43.660 --> 00:03:48.310
It was just that I'm the most nimble and free
to do what's right for my channel.

00:03:48.310 --> 00:03:52.840
If I'm not affiliated with anything else at
a smaller size, I might trade that.

00:03:52.840 --> 00:03:59.060
A advantage for being part of the union right
now, it's simply wouldn't make, but let's

00:03:59.060 --> 00:04:01.580
explore what they're doing because this is
serious.

00:04:01.580 --> 00:04:04.860
This could actually have a really major impact
on youtube.

00:04:04.860 --> 00:04:12.590
The Youtube has union Europe has joined with
Igg metal, which is Germany's largest union

00:04:12.590 --> 00:04:16.650
and Europe's largest trade union to launch
fair tube.

00:04:16.650 --> 00:04:24.039
This is the most significant Youtube Related
Organization of Labor that we have ever seen.

00:04:24.039 --> 00:04:26.190
Here are their demands monetize.

00:04:26.190 --> 00:04:30.919
Everyone bring back monetization for smaller
channels which was taken away disabled.

00:04:30.919 --> 00:04:35.930
The bots at least verified partners have the
right to speak to a real person if you plan

00:04:35.930 --> 00:04:38.039
to remove their channel.

00:04:38.039 --> 00:04:43.279
Transparent content decisions, open up direct
communication between the sensors and the

00:04:43.279 --> 00:04:44.279
creators.

00:04:44.279 --> 00:04:45.279
Pay for the views.

00:04:45.279 --> 00:04:51.300
Stop using demonetized channels as bait to
advertise, monetized channels.

00:04:51.300 --> 00:04:53.020
Stop the monetization as a whole.

00:04:53.020 --> 00:04:57.960
If a video is in line with your rules, allow
ads on an even scale equal treatment for all

00:04:57.960 --> 00:04:58.960
partners.

00:04:58.960 --> 00:05:01.430
Stop preferring some content creators over
others.

00:05:01.430 --> 00:05:07.300
Pay according to delivered values, spread
out the ad money over all youtubers based

00:05:07.300 --> 00:05:09.460
on audience retention, not on ads.

00:05:09.460 --> 00:05:13.050
Next to the content and clarify the rules
block.

00:05:13.050 --> 00:05:17.599
Bring out clear rules with clear examples
about what's okay and what isn't.

00:05:17.599 --> 00:05:22.419
The deadline for Youtube to respond is August
23 so far, no comment from youtube so this

00:05:22.419 --> 00:05:28.629
is really great, but if you look at the list
of demands, you will see that it is all based

00:05:28.629 --> 00:05:36.930
on the connection between ad dollars and content
in the same way that Obamacare did good things,

00:05:36.930 --> 00:05:41.319
but it also further ingrained the for profit
healthcare system that we have by giving tens

00:05:41.319 --> 00:05:44.110
of millions of new customers to for-profit
insurers.

00:05:44.110 --> 00:05:50.979
The demands that are being made here are excellent,
obviously well calibrated demands that reinforce

00:05:50.979 --> 00:05:58.479
the status quo in which content creators are
given dollars via people watching advertising

00:05:58.479 --> 00:06:02.800
funded by advertisers buying an ad contract
with youtube.

00:06:02.800 --> 00:06:04.440
This is only a bandaid.

00:06:04.440 --> 00:06:06.789
This is not a cure for the disease.

00:06:06.789 --> 00:06:12.529
Half of these demands would go away if we
completely reprogrammed how content works,

00:06:12.529 --> 00:06:19.100
if instead of having to make money by having
a video that advertisers say meets their standards

00:06:19.100 --> 00:06:23.759
of what's okay, so that they will run an ad
and give a dollar to youtube from which the

00:06:23.759 --> 00:06:29.969
content creator gets 40 cents or 50 cents
or however much it is, this goes away, which

00:06:29.969 --> 00:06:35.360
is why I've been pushing for us to fund shows
we like directly, period.

00:06:35.360 --> 00:06:37.999
I am supportive of this movement.

00:06:37.999 --> 00:06:42.919
This particular union is not the right thing
for the David Pakman show at this point in

00:06:42.919 --> 00:06:45.110
time, but I want it to succeed.

00:06:45.110 --> 00:06:47.999
But the real way to solve this is separate.

00:06:47.999 --> 00:06:53.770
The ad dollars from the content by funding
shows directly.

00:06:53.770 --> 00:06:58.159
Hundreds and hundreds of you in the last couple
of months have said, I understand the importance

00:06:58.159 --> 00:07:03.100
of that, and you've signed up for memberships,
for example, on our website, www.joinpackman.com

00:07:03.100 --> 00:07:08.409
that severs the tie between advertisers and
our content.

00:07:08.409 --> 00:07:10.280
That is a very good thing.

00:07:10.280 --> 00:07:14.889
Hundreds of you have become patrons donating
as little as a dollar a month to our show

00:07:14.889 --> 00:07:18.360
at patrion.com/david Pakman show.

00:07:18.360 --> 00:07:25.309
I support the union and I wish it wasn't necessary
by changing the system to one where we fund

00:07:25.309 --> 00:07:28.180
directly the programs that we want.

00:07:28.180 --> 00:07:28.270
I hope you'll consider doing that.

